  "evidence": "TEXT_G: Emphasises that the Maastricht-amended Treaty transfers powers to European institutions and that sovereignty-related constitutional changes require public consent; seeks a referendum choice between a “federal Europe” and an association of sovereign nations within a common market; warns of an irreversible federal European state to justify urgency; criticises main parties for limiting any referendum to the single currency, ignoring broader sovereignty questions. TEXT_D: Calls for pro‑European leadership and potential euro entry subject to conditions and referendum; enacts a Bill of Rights, Human Rights Commission, and Freedom of Information; expands equal rights (equal age of consent, repeal Section 28, anti‑discrimination, LGBT/minority protections); pursues ambitious environmental policies (CO2 cuts, pollution tax shift, renewables); advances devolution, PR, and civil liberties safeguards.",
  "reasoning": "TEXT_G argues from TAN commitments by prioritising national sovereignty over supranational authority and mobilising a referendum to defend national decision‑making. TEXT_D argues from GAL commitments—expanding civil liberties and equality, environmentalism, and pro‑EU integration—so the TAN‑leaning electorate profile aligns more closely with TEXT_G.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_G"
}
